Aw, man .... Aissa, you should format your output such that it doesn't get all garbled !

I think that your hunches are correct: you are probably asking too much from the data. Though perhaps you could experiment with the use of solutions from a simpler model as initial values in the likelihood optimisation of a more complex model ? Perhaps these extreme values for the intercepts (essentially 0 or 1 on the probability scale) are just local optima ?

