Dear Aissa,

about your methods/inits question: I really meant to provide as inits solutions (i.e., estimates) from a neighbouring, smaller model. That is, one that may for instance have one covariate less.

Changing the default (?) Nelder-Mead optimisation method to 'BFGS' may also help, perhaps.

Overall, I think that simplification of the model or use of penalized likelihood (or Bayesian inference, which is conceptually similar in a sense) seem to me to be the most promising ways forward.

Best regards  -- Marc

PS: no pb about the 'k' for 'c'. I also mis-write your name, because I can't find the 'trema' on my keyboard ...

